{
  "name": "Day 90 Solution: Content Marketing",
  "description": "Real weekly draft pipeline: Schedule Trigger -> Google Sheets topic queue -> OpenAI draft -> Set status -> Google Sheets update -> Slack review.",
  "tags": [
    "course-solution",
    "WEEK_13",
    "day-90"
  ],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6824729d-2644-4b30-b05f-8503841dfa2d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 90 Solution: Content Marketing\n\nA real weekly draft pipeline: **Schedule Trigger** -> **Google Sheets** reads the topic queue -> **Code** picks the next queued row -> **IF** checks one exists -> **OpenAI** drafts the piece in the right format -> **Set** marks it drafted -> **Google Sheets** writes the status/draft back -> **Slack** sends it for human review before anything publishes.\n\n**Credentials needed to run this for real:** OpenAI API key; Google Sheets (or Airtable) for the topic queue; Slack API for the review notification.\n\n**Matches:** `DAILY_TASKS/DAY_90_Content_Marketing.md`",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 500
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "59120014-e567-4ed3-9fe7-9eb21256d011",
      "name": "10 Real Topics (written)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 10 Real Questions/Objections From This Course\n\n1. Is this too complicated for a non-technical team to maintain?\n2. What happens when the automation silently fails \u2014 will we even know?\n3. How is this different from just using a Zapier template?\n4. What's the real time-to-value \u2014 days or months?\n5. Can we start with one workflow instead of a full overhaul?\n6. How do you price this if our usage varies month to month?\n7. What happens if the API we depend on changes or goes down?\n8. Who owns the workflow once it's built \u2014 us or you?\n9. How do you handle sensitive client data inside the automation?\n10. What's the actual ROI once you strip out the sales pitch?\n\n**4 chosen for this pipeline:** #2 (how-to blog: building failure alerts), #7 (case study: composite client hit by an API outage), #3 (LinkedIn post: silent-failure story), #3 comparison (\"us vs. a generic Zapier template\").",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "80c30ea0-2316-476b-887f-dec88b51629e",
      "name": "Model Written Post",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Model LinkedIn Post (finished piece from this pipeline)\n\n\"I spent 3 hours this week rebuilding a client's lead-routing workflow because their old one silently failed for 6 weeks. No alerts, no logs, nothing.\n\nThe fix wasn't clever \u2014 it was one Slack alert node on the failure path. That's it.\n\nIf your automation doesn't tell you when it breaks, it's not automation. It's a liability with extra steps.\"",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d348e712-ea50-47da-b9c4-6a64184d3501",
      "name": "Weekly Content Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -160,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "weeksInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "60f53128-a0b9-4000-8e7a-e1f281260553",
      "name": "Read Topic Queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        80,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "your_spreadsheet_id",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Topic Queue",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "951a8427-07b7-4747-bc46-0035037d642d",
      "name": "Pick Next Queued Topic",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        320,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const queued = items.filter(i => (i.json.status || '').toString().toLowerCase() === 'queued');\nif (queued.length === 0) {\n  return [{ json: { has_topic: false } }];\n}\nconst next = queued[0].json;\nreturn [{ json: { has_topic: true, row_number: next.row_number, topic: next.topic, format: next.format, status: next.status } }];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c557d7a4-2679-48d1-b9fe-1b17e0021cb1",
      "name": "Has Queued Topic?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        560,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "boolean": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.has_topic }}",
              "value2": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3df8fa5f-a93e-4c7b-8d35-4d6b9b2219b3",
      "name": "Draft Content Piece",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        800,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "operation": "create",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are a ghostwriter for an automation agency. Write a first-pass draft in the requested format, grounded in the given real topic (a client question or objection) \u2014 no generic industry-trend filler, be specific and concrete."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "={{ 'Format: ' + $json.format + '\\nTopic: ' + $json.topic }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.6,
          "maxTokens": 700
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "23ddb5c1-a43f-4c4c-a97a-572dd65915da",
      "name": "Mark Drafted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1040,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "5c1d20af-1083-44f1-afcd-8f77e0e27f06",
              "name": "row_number",
              "value": "={{ $('Pick Next Queued Topic').item.json.row_number }}",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "39663ca5-b90e-4bb4-9625-3c718166490d",
              "name": "topic",
              "value": "={{ $('Pick Next Queued Topic').item.json.topic }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "3ae71d3d-4585-4db7-b0e8-afe9a4c78b17",
              "name": "format",
              "value": "={{ $('Pick Next Queued Topic').item.json.format }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "262a9b8e-4950-462c-b40b-7e7586770538",
              "name": "status",
              "value": "drafted",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "8ba4c38f-82f6-482a-ac81-4951467a92b6",
              "name": "draft_text",
              "value": "={{ $json.message.content }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "9d231c9c-e79e-4e64-a852-3802d97751b8",
              "name": "drafted_at",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b5564129-fcfd-414a-aa1c-54d232f4394d",
      "name": "Update Status in Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        1280,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "your_spreadsheet_id",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Topic Queue",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "row_number": "={{ $json.row_number }}",
            "status": "={{ $json.status }}",
            "draft_text": "={{ $json.draft_text }}",
            "drafted_at": "={{ $json.drafted_at }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7dce72ff-3d70-4686-9c62-094e129eaf2f",
      "name": "Send Draft for Review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1520,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "slackApi",
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "post",
        "channel": "#content-review",
        "text": "={{ 'New draft ready for review \u2014 ' + $json.format + ': ' + $json.topic + '\\n\\n' + $json.draft_text }}",
        "otherOptions": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8ef00880-30ed-4f8f-99b2-c096c0437f9b",
      "name": "No Topics Queued",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        800,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    }
  ],
